  Slug: ratted-out-gun-runner
  DisplayName: Ratted-Out Gun Runner
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/background.svg
  Description: Sure, you've got a checkered past. Who doesn't? It's hard to make
    a living in the City of Smog, so you did what you could to put silvers in your
    pocket and food on the table. You made a good deal of money selling firearms
    from the Gunworks to people who perhaps shouldn't have had them. You even worked
    with wasteland marauders a few times, sticking up Ustradi barges plying the river
    between the Gunworks and Alkenstar. Of course, you never hurt any innocents or
    did anything truly heinous; your criminal career was always just a matter of
    money. One day, a corrupt financier named Ambrost Mugland-a true crook if there
    ever was one-approached you, demanding a cut of your business. When you refused,
    he put in a word with the shieldmarshals that you'd be a certain somewhere at
    a certain time with a certain large quantity of illegally obtained firearms.
    Even though you escaped arrest, your identity was compromised, and your old accomplices
    have all turned their backs on you. Your gun-running days are clearly over. Now,
    you're just running. Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Dexterity or
    Wisdom , and one is a free attribute boost. You're trained in the Stealth skill
    and the Firearm Lore skill. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Experienced
    Smuggler] skill feat.
  SourceTitle: Pathfinder Outlaws of Alkenstar Player's Guide
